# Engineering-first research archive

Start with bus voltage, generator reactive power and branch-end P/Q/MVA, then give necessary equations. Keep physical units and control conditions explicit.

TMM_Transmission_note.md is the evidence-bound research note; story.md is the user-confirmed purpose. The activity profile mirrors the purpose. Write new numerical conclusions only after actual results and manifests are saved.

Use clear statuses: planned, implemented-not-tested, tested-passed, tested-failed, not-run, insufficient. The material check, a registered test count or a template is not scientific evidence.

Old recovery has stopped. Old result numbers and claims must not enter current evidence or new parameter selection. The archive branch can be linked for history.

Use ordinary multivariate t / elliptical only. Existing TMM, ordinary t properties and PV voltage equations are not newly claimed inventions. Current distributions are voltage/angle and branch-end P/Q/MVA; generator Pg/Qg receive matched-input checks and AC-MC summaries, not invented voltage-only TMM curves.

Maintain the note, claims, derivation, symbols, case plan, validation and figure plan when relevant changes occur. Keep author personal configuration out of Git. Applied Energy remains provisional pending evidence.

The new study has no numerical results. Do not write an Abstract or Contributions paragraph claiming validated precision, speed, costs or completed MATLAB localization.
